  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Nettrace: Fix fix to calculation of changetime",
  "description": "A long time ago, in a galaxy far far away, C had arithmetic/logical-\nplus-assignment operators, so that\n\n\ta = a {op} x;\n\ncould be written as\n\n\ta ={op} x;\n\nUnfortunately, if {op} is -, that meant that you could have, for\nexample:\n\n\ta =- 17;\n\nwhich could be interpreted as\n\n\ta = -17;\n\nso they changed the operators to be\n\n\ta {op}= x;\n\nI.e., if you want to subtract 1000 from a variable, do\n\n\telapsed_ms -= 1000;\n\nnot\n\n\telapsed_ms =- 1000;",
